Integration Test Environment
============================

Prerequisites
-------------
- Docker Engine 20.10+ with the Compose plugin (or docker-compose v2)
- The spine repo must build via its top-level Dockerfile

Running
-------
From this directory:

    sh run.sh

The script:
1. Starts MariaDB 10.11 and waits for it to be healthy.
2. Starts snmpsim serving the .snmprec device stubs under snmprec/.
3. Builds the spine container from the repo root Dockerfile.
4. Seeds the Cacti schema (seed.sql) into MariaDB.
5. Runs spine against poller_id=1 host_id=1.
6. Tears down all containers and volumes on exit (pass or fail).

What it tests
-------------
- spine can connect to MariaDB with the test credentials.
- spine queries a fake SNMP device via snmpsim (192.0.2.1, community "public").
- The sysDescr OID (1.3.6.1.2.1.1.1.0) is polled and spine exits 0.

Adding devices
--------------
Drop additional .snmprec files into snmprec/ using the device IP as the
filename (e.g., 192.0.2.2.snmprec). Add matching rows to seed.sql and
re-run.
